1
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:02,500
Thank you, Illinois!

2
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:12,955
Give it up one more time for your next lieutenant governor, christian mitchell!

3
00:00:16,210 --> 00:00:23,810
One of the true delights of running for governor is getting to choose a partner.

4
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:43,920
One of the true delights of running for governor is getting to choose a partner and a leader to run with as Lieutenant Governor.

5
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:48,660
And if I do say so myself, I've hit it out of the park twice now.

6
00:00:49,780 --> 00:01:00,250
And starting tonight, one of them will soon be known as United States senator juliana stratton.

7
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:15,390
Now, there's a woman that I have known for 38 years who has been an unsung champion for the vulnerable and the afflicted.

8
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:21,910
When there's injustice, when people's rights are under attack, she doesn't seek attention.

9
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:25,910
She stands in the breach as an unwavering defender.

10
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,970
She is my best friend.

11
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:31,750
She is the love of my life.

12
00:01:32,490 --> 00:01:35,050
And your first lady, mk Pritzker.

13
00:01:39,879 --> 00:01:46,850
To our daughter, Teddi, and our son, Donny, you have grown into good,

14
00:01:47,030 --> 00:01:50,810
Kind, smart, hard-working adults.

15
00:01:51,630 --> 00:01:55,010
You make mom and me so very proud, and we love you more than life itself.

16
00:01:55,936 --> 00:02:08,120
To every volunteer, every captain and phone banker and canvasser, you've vanquished the mega Illinois GOP.

17
00:02:12,270 --> 00:02:16,010
And you rebuilt the Democratic Party of Illinois.

18
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:23,436
Led by the amazing Chris Shallo.

19
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:28,640
I have the absolute best campaign team in this country.

20
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,520
You all made this victory possible.

21
00:02:32,616 --> 00:02:39,590
And to my opponent, Darren Bailey, who ran hard.

22
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,760
Who ran hard and gave it his all.

23
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:52,700
Despite our differences, I know that we both love Illinois.

24
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:57,960
Mk and I want to wish you and Cindy the blessings of peace in the days ahead.

25
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:00,320
Let's commit.

26
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:10,140
Let's commit to work for a time when all our political disputes will be resolved by the better angels of our nature.

27
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:21,780
Illinois, my heart is full tonight with the kind of emotion that we Midwestern dads too often keep to ourselves.

28
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:33,160
But as I look out at this amazing crowd, I'm reminded how much I love this great state and its people.

29
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:39,360
Your kindness and decency, your work ethic and authenticity.

30
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,920
I love you, too.

31
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:50,920
Your resilience, I am so proud to be governor of Illinois.

32
00:03:55,720 --> 00:04:01,840
I love this patch of prairie land, this union a that built railroads.

33
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:09,550
A state that spawned skyscrapers that split the atom.

34
00:04:11,690 --> 00:04:16,150
I love that Decatur is the soybean capital of the world.

35
00:04:18,072 --> 00:04:22,100
That Morton is the pumpkin capital of the world.

36
00:04:24,230 --> 00:04:28,890
That Collinsville is the horseradish capital of the world.

37
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:39,730
I love that we put mustard on our hot dogs and and we tolerate those who put ketchup on them.

38
00:04:41,330 --> 00:04:42,910
Barely, but still.

39
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:49,290
I love that this is the house where house music started.

40
00:04:57,334 --> 00:05:01,660
I love that the Pope began a journey of faith here.

41
00:05:03,923 --> 00:05:11,118
And he did it by rooting for the white sox.

42
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:18,978
I love that jake and elwood, the Blues Brothers, began their journey in joliet.

43
00:05:21,550 --> 00:05:26,410
I love that a great fire turned Chicago into a hub of entrepreneurs.

44
00:05:27,503 --> 00:05:31,330
And that a great lake made us the home of innovation.

45
00:05:32,088 --> 00:05:40,660
I love that it was the first Illinois president who taught us how to stick together.

46
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:48,740
And that it was another Illinois president who showed us how to hope for better.

47
00:05:55,042 --> 00:06:01,840
I love that over the last 8 years while so much of this country we pledge allegiance to has lost its bearings,

48
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:05,700
Illinoisans have remained steadfast and true.

49
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:14,790
I love that the people here never once fell into the trap of succumbing to the wiles of a petty tyrant.

50
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:25,340
But instead, we recommitted ourselves to the noble precept that democracy and freedom go hand in hand.

51
00:06:25,799 --> 00:06:33,980
An idea that must be renewed, a bedrock that must be reinforced by each generation.

52
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:40,160
I love that we fought when our neighbors needed us to fight.

53
00:06:41,519 --> 00:06:45,560
And that we showed up when we needed to show out.

54
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,980
I love being your governor.

55
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:04,070
I love you, too.

56
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:22,000
Public service is a career path too often belittled.

57
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:32,660
But to do so is to betray the values and hard work of so many people dedicated to making our lives and our communities Better.

58
00:07:33,455 --> 00:07:39,100
From the first responders who run toward danger to the emergency management teams who keep us out of it.

59
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:46,180
From those at the Department of Health who watch for disease to the home health care aids who treat it.

60
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:56,480
From the child welfare case workers who rescue children from neglect to the school social workers who prevent it.

61
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:04,820
Road crews and teachers and conservation experts.

62
00:08:06,015 --> 00:08:11,210
And mental health counselors and librarians.

63
00:08:11,210 --> 00:08:19,350
Every day each of these people demolish the stereotypes ascribed to them.

64
00:08:19,670 --> 00:08:25,090
Every day their public service makes Illinois such a wonderful place to live.

65
00:08:25,790 --> 00:08:31,010
To my staff in the governor's office who have never once flinched.

66
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:39,230
They've never once flinched when forced to confront any crisis they've been asked to endure.

67
00:08:39,650 --> 00:08:44,610
You make me so proud and it's a privilege to work with all of you.

68
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:53,920
Now, the night is still young and we will see what surprises the next few hours hold,

69
00:08:54,540 --> 00:09:02,620
But as I stand here I tell you this, the early results across the country are resuscitating a strange feeling inside of me.

70
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:08,910
It's a feeling of hope.

71
00:09:08,910 --> 00:09:17,640
Because it looks like maybe, just maybe, something is stirring in the conscience of America.

72
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:25,640
My time as governor has been grounded in a somewhat radical idea.

73
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:33,820
Nothing good can be built on the governing notion that the place you want to change is somehow fundamentally irreparable.

74
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:40,000
Hope and fear are from the same family.

75
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:44,500
Both demand that you believe in a future you cannot see.

76
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:48,680
Which one you adopt is a measure of character.

77
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:53,580
In the world right now politicians fall into one of two camps.

78
00:09:53,832 --> 00:09:57,760
Those that ask you to hope and those that want you to fear.

79
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:02,940
For 8 years I've asked you to join me in hope.

80
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:08,160
And I'd like to take a measure tonight of what hope and hard work has gotten us.

81
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:13,180
We've nearly doubled the minimum wage to $15 an hour.

82
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:20,360
We delivered universal paid leave for every Illinois worker.

83
00:10:21,602 --> 00:10:25,740
We have no cell phones in our classrooms.

84
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:31,490
And more teachers in our schools.

85
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:43,160
We require that black history is taught in every school because black history is American history.

86
00:10:47,430 --> 00:10:51,550
And now Illinois has the highest high school graduation rate ever.

87
00:10:55,180 --> 00:11:00,340
We delivered eight balanced budgets that led to 12 state credit upgrades.

88
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:06,520
We built a quantum industry that is shaping up to be the envy of the world.

89
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:12,840
We upgraded our infrastructure entirely with union workers.

90
00:11:16,570 --> 00:11:21,210
We made Illinois a fortress for women's reproductive freedom.

91
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:32,120
We enacted the toughest AI regulations in the country.

92
00:11:32,997 --> 00:11:36,500
We banned assault weapons.

93
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:44,880
We stood up against ICE invasions.

94
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:57,826
And if all of that wasn't good enough for you, well, hope was also given well,

95
00:11:57,826 --> 00:12:01,310
Has given us a winning White sox season.

96
00:12:01,818 --> 00:12:06,460
And a bears playoff win over the packers.

97
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:11,240
And the chicago pope.

98
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:20,148
Now, I can't really take credit for those last three, but I think God has hope in us, Too.

99
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:26,260
Our long list of accomplishments is not to say that the work is done.

100
00:12:27,020 --> 00:12:35,080
I have confidence in our ability to tackle the challenges ahead, but fear has its place in building what is to come.

101
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:38,860
It's just important that we fear the right things.

102
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:43,728
Fear greed.

103
00:12:43,728 --> 00:12:45,020
Fear cruelty.

104
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:47,320
Fear corruption.

105
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:51,980
Fear intolerance and callousness and unchecked power.

106
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:56,440
Fear politics devoid of empathy.

107
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:02,700
Fear any leader who does not appreciate a life filled with simple joys.

108
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:09,340
Who never closed their eyes upon hearing a favorite piece of music.

109
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:15,890
Who never welled up with unselfish pride at a friend's accomplishments.

110
00:13:16,810 --> 00:13:21,430
Who never told a self-deprecating joke just to comfort another.

111
00:13:22,590 --> 00:13:25,850
Who never learned how to apologize simply and sincerely.

112
00:13:26,969 --> 00:13:33,430
Fear any person who doesn't know how to offer compassion when someone they dislike dies.

113
00:13:34,810 --> 00:13:39,550
Or kindness when someone who can't offer them anything needs it.

114
00:13:41,350 --> 00:13:43,510
Those are the things that we should fear.

115
00:13:44,370 --> 00:13:47,390
Those are the people we should fear.

116
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:59,700
We should not fear immigrants and people of color and women.

117
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:04,980
We should not fear the LGBTQ community.

118
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:12,809
We should not fear the weirdos and the weirdoes.

119
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:16,480
And we should not fear the Canadians.

120
00:14:19,030 --> 00:14:27,990
We should not fear the strange, wonderful mix of diverse opinions and backgrounds and ethnicities that make our communities rich,

121
00:14:28,190 --> 00:14:35,270
Our food good, our culture strong, our work ethic durable, and our country so uniquely American.

122
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:43,040
I have one important rule in life.

123
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:47,880
I don't feast with people beside whom I wouldn't trust to starve.

124
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:54,940
And it's always the people who are struggling, who are persecuted, who are unfairly stereotyped,

125
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:58,360
Who would give you the last piece of bread if you needed it.

126
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:02,980
That's the squad with whom I want to roll into the next chapter.

127
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:15,880
Hope for the best in us, fear the worst, and remember that courage doesn't exist without fear.

128
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,440
It exists to confront fear.

129
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:27,580
People have asked me over the last few years what's given me the courage to stand up to this president and to this presidency.

130
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:33,800
They've asked me if I worry about the insults that are flung my way by the Oval Office.

131
00:15:34,695 --> 00:15:39,280
Well, the answer is I don't worry about it at all.

132
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:44,180
I'm happy to be something they cheer because I've seen what they choose to cheer.

133
00:15:48,970 --> 00:15:52,770
There's one question I've gotten a lot over the last few months.

134
00:15:53,530 --> 00:15:54,030
What's next?

135
00:15:55,350 --> 00:15:56,550
The answer is simple.

136
00:15:57,350 --> 00:16:02,510
I'm going to ask you to continue to hope, to wrap yourself in hope,

137
00:16:04,002 --> 00:16:04,971
In courage.

138
00:16:04,971 --> 00:16:11,010
We climbed one mountain tonight, but we are sitting at the base of another.

139
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:17,590
We have a health care system that we need to break down to the studs and rebuild.

140
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:26,080
One where we put doctors and patients ahead of insurance companies and profits.

141
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,360
We have an electoral system that needs real campaign finance reform.

142
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:40,520
Because no special interest should be able to simply buy the regulations they prefer.

143
00:16:41,506 --> 00:16:52,950
We have a growing group of tech robber barons who need to be told that money does not give them the right to exist

144
00:16:52,950 --> 00:16:55,850
Outside the rules we all live by.

145
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:04,260
And we need to rescue the American dream for the next generation.

146
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:17,677
It is simply unacceptable that both the essentials and the joys of living life have moved out of reach for almost every working-class American.

147
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:26,760
This life this one precious, beautiful life needs to be about more than grinding it out every day until the day you die.

148
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:29,040
It's this simple.

149
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:31,940
If you go to work in the morning and you come home at night,

150
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:34,600
You ought to make enough money to put food on the table.

151
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,760
To see a doctor when you're sick.

152
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:42,060
To live in a dignified home.

153
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:44,640
To save for retirement.

154
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:48,380
And take a vacation every once in a while.

155
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:53,100
We can make that happen.

156
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:55,720
We must make that happen.

157
00:17:56,900 --> 00:18:00,620
Now, I know that the last few years have been hard.

158
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:07,060
I know that it would have been easy for you to lose hope along the way.

159
00:18:07,060 --> 00:18:13,520
But at every turn, you've shown the resolve and the courage that hope requires.

160
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:17,580
It's in you as it is in me.

161
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:20,180
Hope lives within us.

162
00:18:22,490 --> 00:18:24,190
Tonight is a good night.

163
00:18:26,490 --> 00:18:28,790
But the work does not end tonight.

164
00:18:29,790 --> 00:18:34,330
Tomorrow we wake up with hope rewarded and purpose renewed.

165
00:18:35,743 --> 00:18:37,870
So I have just one question for you, Illinois.

166
00:18:38,410 --> 00:18:39,710
Are you ready for the fight?

167
00:18:40,717 --> 00:18:42,809
No, I mean it.

168
00:18:42,809 --> 00:18:45,540
Are you ready for the fight?

169
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:53,100
Then go out there with hope and courage and fight like hell for what's next.

170
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:54,360
Thank you.

171
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:58,160
God bless you and God bless the United States.
